MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The packed rows the Spanish words do not fit at the US crops get each language's crops and pieces as data (game_menu.c
LabelCrop tables, the 0183 model): the card list (CARD_LIST_CROPS: Cartas, × Elegir, △ Cancelar, the count's suffix at 0xd8
left blank), the medal screen (MEDAL_VIEW_CROPS: Medallas, Cancelar before drawGlyph's limit), the original chart's keys
(EVO_CHART_KEY_CROPS), the chart detail's Tree and level names (CHART_TREE_CROP, CHART_LEVEL_CROPS: Árbol, Bebé, Infantil,
Novato, Campeón, Perfecto; each centred at dx - 0x44 as the US placed them). English keeps the US values.

The name keyboard (script_menu.c) has Ñ Ü after Z, Á É Í Ó Ú under them, the lower case alike on the right (the digits one
row lower): the mod font's two-byte glyphs, in the cells the US left blank, in both languages. Its labels (Nombre, Borrar,
OK) do not fit 12-pixel cells: the Spanish label row is laid out in pieces (NAMING_CTRL_BOXES, NAMING_LABEL_PIECES per
language; English keeps the US cells), with its colour codes (PIECE_COLORS, font.c drawGlyphPieces) and found on either
page of the box; with the original font that row is drawn in the original's cells instead of the keyboard's. The default
player name is cleared instead of copied from past the end of "BackOK" ([7], which the padded Spanish moved). The memory
card's title gets the player's name in plain Shift-JIS letters (modTitlePlayerName: F040-F057 to their full-width plain
letters), the accented ones kept in the header's reserved bytes after the long names' tail ("A" at [5], a code per
letter) and restored for the save slots (loadSaveSlotData); a name is 2 bytes a letter either way.

readFileSection finds DG.SCN through FILE_OFFSET_TABLE (lookupFileTable: the font's and the language's copy, the sector
build-disc wrote), not CdSearchFile; the cached start is forgotten when the font or the language changes (the Spanish and
the original-font DG.SCN copies were never read: the dialogue stayed English)

